"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2015-08-04T21:02:24Z","updated_at":"2019-09-06T23:20:30Z","closed_at":"2015-08-07T08:58:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"2 weeks ago, we started running unit tests in a new HTML Document, see: https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/modules/angular2/src/test_lib/test_injector.ts#L96\nIf it works fine in Chrome, it creates problems in other browsers.\n\nThe biggest one is for Safari where events are not dispatched in such a document. This causes the 26 events-based unit tests to fail there.\nIt also generates one failure in Firefox and IE11. In Firefox, the default behaviour of an event is not applied (e.g. checkbox not checked after a click). In IE11, text selection feature doesn\"t work.\n\nMoving back to the real DOM doesn't seem to degrade performances, but it means loosing the isolation that is brought by a new Document. But it seems needed to be able to integrate these browsers to CI.\n","closed_by":{"login":"marclaval","id":2316643,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTY2NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2316643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval","html_url":"https://github.com/marclaval","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marclaval/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ma